o we have no feedback openness info.\n\nWe need to decide whether this new evidence changes our view. Perhaps D's decision quality is strong, but still concerns about crew cooperation and communication. B still seems best overall, but we might consider D as stronger alternative now that we have decision quality evidence. However we still lack feedback openness for D, and we have concerns about arrogance and weak leadership, which affect crew cooperation.\n\nThus we can argue that while D shows strong decision quality, the lack of evidence on feedback openness and the known arrogance/weak leadership still make B preferable, especially since B's cooperation issues can be mitigated. So we maintain recommendation for B.\n\nWe need to reference James's tool answer and prior discussion. Provide explicit facts: D solves problems extremely well, responds adequately to unexpected events; D is regarded as arrogant, weak leadership, hot temper. B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good technical, but uncooperative, grumpy. So we argue B still best.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
